    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass (0 failures, 0 errors), including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`. The `ERROR GeneralExceptionHandler` line in the logs is an expected escalation from a test that deliberately triggers an error path, not a test failure.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `householdId` is now deterministic \u2014 the first 12 UPPER-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` \u2014 so owners sharing lastName and postcode automatically resolve to the same household. Four files changed plus documentation:\n\n**`AssignOwnerHousehold.java`** \u2014 Rewrote it to *always* compute the household id from the owner's normalized lastName and postcode (no longer conditional on `sharesHousehold`, no longer scans/mutates other owners). No-ops when there's no postcode (household of one), which keeps the seed owners (all null postcode) and the `Franklin`-with-no-postcode V1 tests from colliding.\n\n**`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 Now takes `@Val OwnerFieldsDto request` and rejects two cases with 409:\n- **Household duplicate**: an existing owner shares the computed `householdId` \u2192 rejected *unless* `sharesHousehold` is set (in which case the owner is admitted as a declared additional member).\n- **Exact identity duplicate**: full `identityKey` match \u2014 still applies (covers no-postcode owners) and is never bypassed.\n\n**`AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 Now takes `@Val OwnerFieldsDto request` and returns early when `sharesHousehold` is true: a declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\n\n`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize` needed no change \u2014 it already keys the household-size snapshot (which feeds the membership level) off `owner.getHouseholdId()`, which is now the deterministic value.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 Updated the `owners.POST.yml` step comments and the `openapi.yml` descriptions for `householdId` and `sharesHousehold` to match the new behaviour.\n\n`sharesHousehold` now only bypasses the duplicate block rather than creating the link, exactly as specified.",
